{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"5bf88d86e08cb8fd3c476117b6a7f9861d74b2e98d7a873bc37a60b4d18a4691","digest":{"component_or_area":"store git operations","key_entities":["_with_index_lock_retry","_store_git_op_lock","run_git_write","_commands/compact.py","_commands/delete.py","_commands/fsck.py","_commands/txn.py","_store/event_append.py","metrics/blame.py","metrics/git_metrics.py","_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S","_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT","rebar-git-op.lock"],"problem_keywords":["local git lock contention","concurrent store writes","index.lock","ref locks","bounded retry","jittered backoff","advisory locking","watchdog timeouts"],"propositions":["Local git call sites in rebar are unbounded and lack contention policy, causing errors under high concurrent agent load.","Transient git lock conflicts on index.lock and ref locks should be absorbed silently via bounded jittered retry without escalating to the calling agent.","A per-store advisory lock plus jittered exponential backoff on git operations resolves contention automatically, with only genuinely stuck locks (budget exhausted) surfacing one actionable error naming the lock file.","All local git call sites must be explicitly bounded with watchdog timeouts (120s for writes/plumbing, 300s for metrics) or documented as deliberately unbounded, to prevent one hung mount from stalling every agent."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787471986911814001,"uuid":"a219b86a-c32a-40ff-9943-ebb0fcc90068"}